          "description": "What is a shotgun house?\n\nIt is a house in which each room stands directly behind the room in front of it.\n\nFor Example: living room | Kitchen Dining room | Bedroom\n\nOur house had two rooms as follows:\n\n The first was the living-room/bedroom, and the second was the kitchen/dining-room. A third room was planned but never built.\n\nIn the 1930's during the depression, there were many &quot;Shot gun houses&quot; in the west Kern county. Our house is furnished as it would have been in the depression era. There were no locks on the Door, for no one stole then.\n\nWe know this house started life as a ten house for this piece of canvas and other pieces like it were hanging in the windows.\na copy of a newspaper dated October 1911 was found uner the old linoleum.\n\n",
